Round 1 will isolate two claims against the known baseline:

- H1: under the short 6-second horizon, unit sparse bonuses underweight the actual objective; increasing engagement to 3 and success to 8 should improve terminal success without changing the dense landscape.
- H2: aggregate keypoint distance conflates lateral alignment, yaw, and depth; adding always-on lateral proximity plus a depth term activated only inside a 6 mm lateral corridor should reduce unsafe premature descent and improve insertion.

Both retain the original three keypoint terms and epoch 50, so the comparison has a clear baseline interpretation.
