codex
Round 2 rejects both refinements: the 3 mm hard gate scored 515/1024 (0.50293), and smooth coupling scored 509/1024 (0.49707), both below the 6 mm hard gate’s 544/1024. The result suggests the discontinuous corridor is useful as an attainable phase-entry bonus, while 3 mm makes that credit too sparse.

Round 3 will test the two most direct implications: widen the phase-entry corridor modestly to 8 mm, and independently retain 6 mm while increasing only depth weight from 2 to 3.
