codex
Round 4 rejects signed monotonic depth (503/1024, 0.49121) but supports bounded reward memory: prior-distance progress reaches 551/1024 (0.53809), a new best and +7 over the memoryless 6 mm recipe. The gain is modest but deterministic under the fixed protocol.

Round 5 will bracket the memory coefficient around 100 while holding every other node fixed: weight 50 versus 200. This tests whether progress credit is helping gently or whether stronger immediate credit can improve sample efficiency further.
