Round 6 shows training is still improving late: epoch 45 scores 500/1024 (0.48828), epoch 49 scores 529/1024 (0.51660), both below epoch 50’s 551/1024. I’ll retain epoch 50.

The next structural opportunity is the exact lateral predicate. Engagement only becomes visible after both centering and descent, while the terminal criterion requires `xy < 2.5 mm`. Round 7 will add an explicit centered-at-any-height phase bonus to the best graph, testing weights 0.5 and 1.0. This should teach precise lateral placement before contact without changing depth shaping.
