codex
Round 30 confirms the inherited engagement weight 1: weights 0.5 and 1.5 score 458/1024 and 502/1024.

I’ll test a new structural hypothesis aimed at the wide resets: before lateral alignment, the original keypoint reward can encourage premature descent. Round 31 adds an explicit hover-height reward only outside the 6 mm corridor, then turns it off for insertion. Candidate hover targets are 30 mm and 40 mm above the hole base; this should teach “align above, then descend.”
